From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000010 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: polyregion <noreply@polyregion>
Date: Tue, 06 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [SPIRV] deduce cmpxchg pointee from the compared value

The cmpxchg result is the { T, i1 } pair, so using it as the known element
type of the pointer operand records an aggregate pointee and makes the
pointer-cast legaliser insert a ptrcast that it cannot rewrite for
spv_cmpxchg. Use the compared value's type, as atomicrmw already does with
its value operand.

Not upstream as of llvm/llvm-project main (2026-10-09); the open
llvm/llvm-project#202098 fixes the same crash on the legaliser side by
rewriting atomic users of a ptrcast.
---
--- a/llvm/lib/Target/SPIRV/SPIRVEmitIntrinsics.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/Target/SPIRV/SPIRVEmitIntrinsics.cpp
@@ -1242,9 +1242,10 @@
     Ops.push_back(std::make_pair(Ref->getPointerOperand(),
                                  StoreInst::getPointerOperandIndex()));
   } else if (auto *Ref = dyn_cast<AtomicCmpXchgInst>(I)) {
-    KnownElemTy = isPointerTy(I->getType())
+    Type *ValueTy = Ref->getCompareOperand()->getType();
+    KnownElemTy = isPointerTy(ValueTy)
                       ? getAtomicElemTy(GR, I, Ref->getPointerOperand())
-                      : I->getType();
+                      : ValueTy;
     if (!KnownElemTy)
       return;
     Incomplete = isTodoType(Ref->getPointerOperand());
